<title>UK: Allied Domecq up on LVMH speculation.</title>
<headline>Allied Domecq up on LVMH speculation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares Allied Domecq Plc rose in a mostly lower UK equity market on Monday, as a press report renewed talk of a possible link with LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton of France, dealers said.</p>
<p>Allied shares -- which have underperformed the rest of the UK equity market this year -- were up 6p at 441-1/2 by 1141 GMT in modest volume of 805,282 shares.  </p>
<p>The Sunday Times said Allied could link with LVMH if the French group was unsuccessful in its attempt to persuade Guinness Plc and Grand Metropolitan Plc to abandon their alliance and instead pursue a three-way drinks merger.</p>
<p>Allied declined comment on what it said was no more than market speculation.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
